why Every Alliance quest of the Deadmines in one run, with the Defias Brotherhood and Alba Fairmoon's chains.

# The Deadmines' Alliance quests in one guide: Gnoarn in Ironforge, the
# pick-ups in Stormwind, the Defias Brotherhood chain and Alba Fairmoon's
# chain between Westfall, Redridge and Stormwind, one run through the mines,
# then the hand-ins. Steps already done are passed over, so the guide picks up
# wherever the chain stands.
#
# The chains:
# - Gryan Stoutmantle's 65 The Defias Brotherhood (to Wiley the Black) -> 132
#   -> 135 (to Master Mathias Shaw) -> 141 -> 142 (A Mysterious Message) ->
#   the Defias Traitor's 155 -> 166 (VanCleef's head); Scout Riell's 214 Red
#   Silk Bandanas opens after 155.
# - Alba Fairmoon's 92742 Testing the Wells and 92744 Murloc Gills -> 92745
#   The State of the Mines -> 92747 Moonbrook Espionage -> 92748 Explosive
#   Consultation (to Sprite Jumpsprocket) -> 92749 A Dynamite Plan and 92750,
#   92751 Detonation at a Distance (Jasper Fel) -> 92752 -> 92753
#   Destruction in Deadmines (the explosives by the forge inside) -> 92819
#   (the Detonator at the mines' exit).
# - Wilder Thistlenettle's 168 Collecting Memories and 167 Oh Brother...;
#   Gnoarn's 2041 Speak with Shoni -> 2040 Underground Assault (Sneed's
#   Shredder's Gnoam Sprecklesprocket); VanCleef's An Unsent Letter (item
#   2874) starts 373, for Baros Alexston.
#
# Left out: the Paladins' 1654 and 1806 The Test of Righteousness, whose chain
# needs Jordan's Hammer from Shadowfang Keep. The Unsent Letter's follow-up,
# 389 Bazil Thredd, opens the Stockade's quests and is in the Stockade guide.
# No Horde guide: the Horde's one quest here, the Scourge Paladins' 95036 A
# Moon-Kissed Blade, wants three items the data gives no source for.
#
# Inside: nothing in the data places the bosses or the forge inside, so their
# goals stand at the door (@41.9,72.8, Westfall) with `group 5`. The bosses
# come in the order of the client's dungeon journal (Rhahk'Zor, Sneed, Miner
# Johnson, Gilnid, Captain Greenskin, Mr. Smite, Cookie, Edwin VanCleef), not
# of a recorded run. Every quest goal is counted by the quest log, so a group
# that takes them in another order still gets each step ticked.
#
# Sources (facts only):
# - Quests, NPCs, items, objects and rewards: Polestar's reference data
#   (data/forever, built from QuestieDB Forever 1.1.4) and Polestar 0.4.1.1's
#   Codex page for the dungeon. The escort's end and the Detonator's spot are
#   the data's; Rough Dynamite has no source there (an engineer's make).
# - The door: players' recordings, as Polestar's Codex holds them
#   (data/codex/entrances.json).
# - The dungeon's size, levels and bosses: the client's group finder and
#   dungeon journal, as Polestar's Codex page holds them (five players, levels
#   17 to 26).
# INGAME: where inside is the forge for Destruction in Deadmines?

